The following changes have been made to XHost since version 1.10:

Thanks go out to Ricardo Molinar for bug reports and helpful
suggestions.

New features:

- "List conferences" and "Join conference" commands were added to the
default sysop menu.

- A new default menu is provided in the file QDMENU.ZIP. It is designed
to imitate Telix's QDHOST menu.

Bug fixes:

- If a user answered 'No' to the ANSI color prompt, the foreground color
  would be set to red if the previous user had color turned on.

- After a local logon, the script would not reinitialize the modem into
auto-answer mode. This was corrected.

- The sysop's color bit was not being used during a quick logon.

- The user editor would run into some trouble if no users were on file
and it was attempted to edit a user without adding one first using (+).

- The title screen would overwrite the status bar if it was on top of
the screen. The user editor and file adder had similar glitches.

- The system password was displayed as it was typed at the beginning of
Setup. Its color was changed to blue on blue to avoid this.

- There was some confusion in the documentation regarding the name of
the custom menus for file lists, text files and doors. It is now
consistent.

- More documentation was added regarding text files and the user flags
(registration, scan) associated with conferences.

- Conferences with no file directory #1 defined will not accept uploads.


The following changes have been made to XHost since version 1.00:

New features:

- The editor now has a quote function.

- Users now can toggle whether to import FILE_ID.DIZ description files
  into the file list. Accordingly, the file list can now support 10
  lines of description at 46 characters per line. This wasn't really my
  idea, but a request by Stephen Nix.

- A "Change page length" command is now available in the Info & Setup
  menu.

Bug fixes:

- Some entries were missing from the default menus: Doors and List
  contents of EXTRACT.

- The "Move file" command called PACK.EXE with incorrect parameters.

- 'Forced' private messages (ie comments, replies to private messages)
  were not being marked as private.

- The script now hangs up properly. A flag had the wrong value, causing
  the routine to be skipped completely.

- Fixed problem with chat greeting to users with names of one word.

- Added some pauses to the end of the archive handling functions.

- The upload directory is now correctly set to the first file dir in
  the current conference.

- In many cases, the full-screen editor would fail to save the current
  line before a function was executed (redraw, help). This is fixed.

- The messages which had replies weren't correctly displayed as such.
